1
00:00:00,001 --> 00:00:01,022
(All characters, locations,
and events are fictional

2
00:00:01,047 --> 00:00:02,022
and for entertainment
purposes only.

3
00:00:02,047 --> 00:00:02,998
No actions depicted are intended
to be encouraged or endorsed.

4
00:00:03,023 --> 00:00:03,990
Animals were specially trained
and supervised by professionals.

5
00:00:04,015 --> 00:00:04,994
Viewer discretion is advised.)

6
00:00:05,081 --> 00:00:07,871
Golf teaches us that
no day is ever perfect.

7
00:00:13,136 --> 00:00:15,855
But every day
can still end beautifully.

8
00:00:15,880 --> 00:00:18,761
Some holes are pars, while others
we may go a little over.

9
00:00:19,930 --> 00:00:21,457
But if we make it all the way
to the 18th hole

10
00:00:21,482 --> 00:00:24,061
with a steady heart
and a steadfast spirit,

11
00:00:26,197 --> 00:00:27,954
then it's been a good day.

12
00:00:28,829 --> 00:00:30,784
And when it comes to
relationships,

13
00:00:30,809 --> 00:00:33,532
no matter what we go through,
all we need is someone to stay

14
00:00:33,557 --> 00:00:37,885
and say, "Are you tired?
Thank you for today."

15
00:00:37,910 --> 00:00:41,062
Because in the end, life isn't
a competition to beat anyone.

16
00:00:41,617 --> 00:00:44,743
It's about playing a round
with someone who makes you feel

17
00:00:44,768 --> 00:00:46,999
that no matter
how tough the hole,

18
00:00:47,696 --> 00:00:49,047
you'll still want to start over,

19
00:00:49,071 --> 00:00:51,366
hold hands,
and walk into tomorrow together.

20
00:00:55,573 --> 00:01:02,408
(Pro Arm - Arthitaya Kunalaphat)

21
00:01:08,456 --> 00:01:12,025
♪ Everyone can tell
by the way you stare ♪

22
00:01:12,668 --> 00:01:14,313
♪ Sneaking little looks
when I'm unaware ♪

23
00:01:14,338 --> 00:01:18,095
♪ It's plain to see ♪

24
00:01:18,120 --> 00:01:20,183
♪ I know exactly
what you think of me ♪

25
00:01:20,252 --> 00:01:23,688
♪ First to watch my stories
every time ♪

26
00:01:24,285 --> 00:01:26,078
♪ You remember
every fave of mine ♪

27
00:01:26,103 --> 00:01:29,940
♪ Everywhere I go,
you're by my side ♪

28
00:01:29,967 --> 00:01:31,797
♪ Don't tell me
there's nothing on your mind ♪

29
00:01:31,821 --> 00:01:34,669
♪ So when are you
gonna say the words? ♪

30
00:01:34,694 --> 00:01:36,574
♪ Don't keep me waiting
till it hurts ♪

31
00:01:36,599 --> 00:01:39,411
♪ The way you act,
I know you're into me ♪

32
00:01:39,436 --> 00:01:42,330
♪ That racing heart
gives you away so easily ♪

33
00:01:42,355 --> 00:01:46,155
♪ But I'll play clueless,
just wait and see ♪

34
00:01:46,180 --> 00:01:48,180
♪ I wanna hear you say it to me ♪

35
00:01:48,205 --> 00:01:50,907
♪ Giving me signs,
so why still wait? ♪

36
00:01:50,932 --> 00:01:54,438
♪ You know I'm into you, I bet ♪

37
00:01:54,463 --> 00:01:59,232
♪ How long will you keep
playing so tough? ♪

38
00:01:59,257 --> 00:02:01,204
♪ Or should I be the one
to call your bluff? ♪

39
00:02:03,037 --> 00:02:05,263
Today's main agenda is

40
00:02:05,288 --> 00:02:09,538
the All Star Women's
Golf Tournament.

41
00:02:09,904 --> 00:02:11,869
The Golf Course Network
is organizing

42
00:02:11,894 --> 00:02:13,606
the All Star Women's
Golf Tournament.

43
00:02:13,630 --> 00:02:17,548
So I was thinking of sending you
to represent Goodview.

44
00:02:17,573 --> 00:02:19,163
I'd rather not compete.

45
00:02:19,188 --> 00:02:20,202
Why not?

46
00:02:20,227 --> 00:02:22,085
There are some things
I'd rather not explain.

47
00:02:22,110 --> 00:02:25,126
What happened that day has stayed
with Vee all this time.

48
00:02:25,169 --> 00:02:27,281
It was the final day
of the tournament.

49
00:02:27,306 --> 00:02:29,180
Her father had a heart attack.

50
00:02:29,205 --> 00:02:31,205
By the time
Vee got to the hospital,

51
00:02:31,949 --> 00:02:33,269
it was too late.

52
00:02:50,522 --> 00:02:52,068
You want me to compete

53
00:02:52,855 --> 00:02:55,133
because you want our course
to become famous again, right?

54
00:02:55,319 --> 00:02:57,005
You want everything
to go perfectly,

55
00:02:57,030 --> 00:02:58,861
just like you planned.

56
00:02:59,036 --> 00:03:01,210
But my golfing career

57
00:03:01,586 --> 00:03:03,532
was never that beautiful.

58
00:03:04,492 --> 00:03:07,258
Everything fell apart the day
I chose the trophy

59
00:03:07,809 --> 00:03:09,243
instead of my father.

60
00:03:41,519 --> 00:03:44,249
And now you're asking me
to choose again.

61
00:03:44,749 --> 00:03:46,852
Between my pain

62
00:03:47,757 --> 00:03:49,542
and your success.

63
00:03:51,487 --> 00:03:54,316
And you should know
what I'll choose.

64
00:04:19,107 --> 00:04:20,734
Hello, Pro Vee.

65
00:04:23,358 --> 00:04:24,373
Hello.

66
00:04:25,450 --> 00:04:27,550
I just finished my lesson
with Pro Wan.

67
00:04:27,827 --> 00:04:30,415
I've gotten a lot better lately.

68
00:04:30,440 --> 00:04:32,071
I'll probably be ready
for a round soon.

69
00:04:32,639 --> 00:04:37,296
It'd be great if I could play
my first round with you, Pro Vee.

70
00:04:39,650 --> 00:04:42,692
Are you free, Pro Vee?
Want to grab something to eat?

71
00:04:42,717 --> 00:04:45,885
I'm sorry,
but I already have plans.

72
00:04:47,723 --> 00:04:50,161
You really have plans?

73
00:04:50,186 --> 00:04:52,808
Or are you turning me down

74
00:04:53,141 --> 00:04:54,673
because you're worried about Nana?

75
00:04:56,216 --> 00:04:58,558
- Um...
- I can tell.

76
00:04:58,917 --> 00:05:04,627
Well, you two are way too close
for a course owner and a pro.

77
00:05:04,882 --> 00:05:08,131
Even the grass on the green
can tell.

78
00:05:12,225 --> 00:05:13,313
Pro Vee.

79
00:05:14,687 --> 00:05:17,219
Can I be honest with you
about something?

80
00:05:20,814 --> 00:05:24,181
I've been thinking long and hard
about whether I should say this,

81
00:05:24,206 --> 00:05:26,919
but I'd feel terrible
if I didn't tell you.

82
00:05:28,818 --> 00:05:30,061
Tell me what?

83
00:05:31,608 --> 00:05:32,791
It's about Nana.

84
00:05:34,264 --> 00:05:40,769
The truth is, Nana never had
serious feelings for you.

85
00:05:41,910 --> 00:05:44,321
When she told us

86
00:05:44,346 --> 00:05:46,689
about having to manage
this course,

87
00:05:47,498 --> 00:05:52,648
Wow, you've got quite
the list of plans, Miss Nana.

88
00:05:52,673 --> 00:05:54,912
Yeah. You think
you can handle it?

89
00:05:54,937 --> 00:05:56,819
The course is huge.

90
00:05:56,844 --> 00:05:58,806
You've got so much to deal with.

91
00:05:59,178 --> 00:06:00,808
I've got Nut to help me.

92
00:06:01,952 --> 00:06:03,755
Can Nut handle all that
on his own?

93
00:06:03,780 --> 00:06:04,977
Exactly.

94
00:06:05,519 --> 00:06:07,130
Let me tell you,

95
00:06:07,155 --> 00:06:09,942
you need to put that irresistible
charm of yours to use.

96
00:06:09,967 --> 00:06:13,463
Win over the people you think
can help you the most.

97
00:06:14,590 --> 00:06:15,828
How, Meow?

98
00:06:17,202 --> 00:06:20,136
If that person
falls for your charm,

99
00:06:20,743 --> 00:06:23,782
they'll do anything for you.

100
00:06:24,364 --> 00:06:27,557
Not because it's their job
or because they're getting paid,

101
00:06:27,863 --> 00:06:30,327
but because they genuinely
want to help you.

102
00:06:30,995 --> 00:06:34,635
Get four or five people like that
at the course, and you're set.

103
00:06:35,295 --> 00:06:36,350
Really?

104
00:06:36,703 --> 00:06:40,250
Just work that charm of yours,
you little heiress.

105
00:06:42,071 --> 00:06:44,914
Then start with that golf pro
you told us about.

106
00:07:02,179 --> 00:07:04,918
I never thought
Nana would actually do it.

107
00:07:06,555 --> 00:07:09,505
I don't want to see you take her
seriously all by yourself.

108
00:07:10,174 --> 00:07:12,041
You're a good person, Pro Vee.

109
00:07:12,066 --> 00:07:14,979
You shouldn't be
used as someone's pawn.

110
00:07:16,382 --> 00:07:18,792
I don't want to see you
get hurt in the end.

111
00:07:32,834 --> 00:07:34,151
This pen is great, Belle.

112
00:07:34,176 --> 00:07:36,152
I've signed so many papers
and my hand doesn't even hurt.

113
00:07:36,177 --> 00:07:38,862
And it comes in so many colors.
Love it.

114
00:07:43,778 --> 00:07:44,996
Thank you.

115
00:07:46,440 --> 00:07:47,916
I'm actually
pretty excited, Belle.

116
00:07:50,211 --> 00:07:52,972
You think
it'll turn out well, right?

117
00:07:53,695 --> 00:07:54,956
Of course.

118
00:07:55,346 --> 00:07:58,661
Everyone's already more than
halfway through the preparations.

119
00:07:58,686 --> 00:08:01,145
Everyone knows
this All Star tournament

120
00:08:01,170 --> 00:08:04,729
will be another event that
puts our course back on the map.

121
00:08:04,994 --> 00:08:07,512
And if Pro Vee
wins the championship,

122
00:08:07,537 --> 00:08:10,363
we'll get to host
an Asian Tour event.

123
00:08:10,388 --> 00:08:12,402
That would put us
on the map across Asia.

124
00:08:14,711 --> 00:08:17,299
Pro Vee still hasn't agreed
to represent our course.

125
00:08:17,793 --> 00:08:18,816
Oh.

126
00:08:19,298 --> 00:08:21,392
But a lot of people are trying
to convince her.

127
00:08:23,449 --> 00:08:25,563
And if it's not Pro Vee,

128
00:08:25,588 --> 00:08:27,271
who would you choose, Miss Nana?

129
00:08:28,113 --> 00:08:29,573
I haven't thought that far ahead.

130
00:08:30,347 --> 00:08:32,975
Oh, have you talked to Pro Jin?

131
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:35,270
How's she doing over
at the Royal Green?

132
00:08:35,899 --> 00:08:38,891
Mm, she's doing okay.
I heard that lately...

133
00:08:41,062 --> 00:08:43,422
Are you busy, Nana?
I have a plan to pitch.

134
00:08:43,447 --> 00:08:45,520
I want the pro who's competing
in the All Star

135
00:08:45,545 --> 00:08:47,856
to help test out our golf game.

136
00:08:48,158 --> 00:08:49,864
It could help promote it, too.

137
00:08:49,896 --> 00:08:51,607
Do you have 20 minutes
to hear me out?

138
00:08:51,632 --> 00:08:52,663
Sure, Gus.

139
00:08:53,393 --> 00:08:55,004
I'll leave you two to it, then.

140
00:08:57,962 --> 00:08:59,481
Okay, let's hear it.

141
00:08:59,829 --> 00:09:02,530
It's about the latest technology
being used in golf,

142
00:09:02,555 --> 00:09:04,784
like distance-measuring tech.

143
00:09:12,009 --> 00:09:13,017
Pro Vee.

144
00:09:14,747 --> 00:09:16,239
Can I talk to you for a minute?

145
00:09:17,405 --> 00:09:20,136
Is it about competing
in the All Star?

146
00:09:20,810 --> 00:09:21,896
Yes.

147
00:09:21,929 --> 00:09:23,958
Nana said you haven't agreed yet,

148
00:09:24,533 --> 00:09:25,605
so I thought...

149
00:09:25,630 --> 00:09:27,949
You thought
it'd be good for the course

150
00:09:27,974 --> 00:09:30,663
and good for me, right?

151
00:09:35,506 --> 00:09:38,616
But I respect
whatever decision you make.

152
00:09:40,580 --> 00:09:43,375
Pro Vee, you have a visitor.

153
00:09:43,670 --> 00:09:47,156
Okay. I'll excuse myself for now.

154
00:09:59,747 --> 00:10:02,544
What's wrong? Why did you come
all the way to the course?

155
00:10:06,387 --> 00:10:08,648
I made
your favorite chicken soup.

156
00:10:08,673 --> 00:10:10,172
I brought some for Nana, too.

157
00:10:11,139 --> 00:10:14,509
Someone asked you to come
talk to me about the All Star?

158
00:10:18,929 --> 00:10:20,414
I understand you, Vee.

159
00:10:21,112 --> 00:10:23,335
But it happened a long time ago.

160
00:10:24,418 --> 00:10:28,469
But to me, Mom, it feels like
it just happened yesterday.

161
00:10:29,195 --> 00:10:30,226
Vee...

162
00:10:31,823 --> 00:10:34,967
How long are you going to stay
stuck in that moment?

163
00:10:35,518 --> 00:10:38,537
And if I compete this time,

164
00:10:39,492 --> 00:10:41,492
what will
I have to lose again, Mom?

165
00:10:41,974 --> 00:10:43,941
But just because
you don't compete

166
00:10:44,314 --> 00:10:47,711
doesn't mean you won't
lose anything, sweetheart.

167
00:10:48,952 --> 00:10:50,273
What do you mean?

168
00:10:52,495 --> 00:10:55,474
You're going to lose the
opportunities life has to offer.

169
00:10:55,895 --> 00:10:59,488
What happened that day
made you close yourself off

170
00:10:59,513 --> 00:11:01,513
from going any further.

171
00:11:01,999 --> 00:11:03,556
Think about it, sweetheart.

172
00:11:05,167 --> 00:11:06,587
Deep down,

173
00:11:07,614 --> 00:11:11,035
what is your ultimate goal
on your journey in golf?

174
00:11:13,934 --> 00:11:16,236
And what is your goal in life?

175
00:11:17,124 --> 00:11:19,124
What you're doing right now,

176
00:11:19,590 --> 00:11:21,533
when will it get you there?

177
00:11:22,217 --> 00:11:23,836
And most importantly,

178
00:11:25,490 --> 00:11:27,493
what is your heart
telling you now?

179
00:11:28,398 --> 00:11:30,080
What is it telling you to do?

180
00:11:31,185 --> 00:11:32,768
And who are you doing it for?

181
00:11:57,323 --> 00:11:59,090
- Chef Queen.
- Yes?

182
00:11:59,115 --> 00:12:01,115
Have you seen Pro Vee today?

183
00:12:01,483 --> 00:12:04,737
Oh, Pro Vee should be teaching
a lesson today.

184
00:12:07,850 --> 00:12:13,238
Ooh, why does the mood feel
so gloomy today?

185
00:12:13,474 --> 00:12:14,679
Did you two have a fight?

186
00:12:15,488 --> 00:12:17,193
Like tongue and teeth,

187
00:12:17,218 --> 00:12:19,637
people living together
are bound to clash.

188
00:12:19,903 --> 00:12:22,853
When you're in love.
Oh, take it easy, talk it out.

189
00:12:22,878 --> 00:12:24,602
A word or two and you'll make up.

190
00:12:24,627 --> 00:12:25,753
Oh!

191
00:12:26,283 --> 00:12:28,469
Did I just say "in love"?

192
00:12:28,494 --> 00:12:30,980
Wait, did I say that right?

193
00:12:31,005 --> 00:12:33,094
How did that just slip out?

194
00:12:33,119 --> 00:12:35,119
Was that even right?

195
00:12:35,144 --> 00:12:38,263
You know,
love is like a raging bull.

196
00:12:38,288 --> 00:12:41,466
When it gets late at night...
Hey, Miss!

197
00:12:43,529 --> 00:12:45,918
You act like I'm invisible!

198
00:12:46,323 --> 00:12:49,086
I'm all alone. I'm lonely.

199
00:12:49,111 --> 00:12:51,423
You come around,
then you disappear.

200
00:12:51,448 --> 00:12:53,448
And then
there's no one here at all.

201
00:12:53,623 --> 00:12:56,482
Who brought me flowers?
Thank you!

202
00:13:19,263 --> 00:13:20,398
Pro Vee.

203
00:13:22,274 --> 00:13:24,123
There's something
I want to talk to you about.

204
00:13:24,497 --> 00:13:26,340
- Well...
- I've decided.

205
00:13:26,928 --> 00:13:29,872
I'll represent our course
in the All Star tournament.

206
00:13:33,815 --> 00:13:35,032
What do you mean?

207
00:13:36,405 --> 00:13:38,525
I'm going to compete
in the All Star.

208
00:13:38,550 --> 00:13:41,872
But there's something
I want to ask you.

209
00:13:42,811 --> 00:13:44,033
What is it?

210
00:13:44,610 --> 00:13:48,821
Fahsai told me that the reason
you've been so nice to me

211
00:13:48,846 --> 00:13:50,506
was because
you were trying to charm me,

212
00:13:50,720 --> 00:13:52,707
so you could use me.

213
00:13:52,732 --> 00:13:55,024
But I don't believe that.

214
00:13:55,049 --> 00:13:57,667
I just want to hear you say
that's not true.

215
00:13:57,692 --> 00:13:59,914
I would never do
something like that.

216
00:14:00,229 --> 00:14:02,938
You know
how real what we have is.

217
00:14:03,895 --> 00:14:07,221
And about wanting you
to compete again,

218
00:14:08,309 --> 00:14:10,494
I understand
you were only trying to help.

219
00:14:10,722 --> 00:14:14,403
And I want to thank you for
making me see things differently.

220
00:14:16,807 --> 00:14:19,141
I want to apologize to you, too.

221
00:14:19,737 --> 00:14:22,285
I was a little too harsh
that day.

222
00:14:23,731 --> 00:14:25,227
A little?

223
00:14:25,252 --> 00:14:27,647
But it did make me
realize some things.

224
00:14:28,122 --> 00:14:31,813
Let's just say everything happens
for a reason.

225
00:14:31,838 --> 00:14:33,170
Have you heard that before?

226
00:14:35,594 --> 00:14:39,962
Vee, I don't want you to think
that by competing again,

227
00:14:40,283 --> 00:14:41,765
you're doing it for the course,

228
00:14:41,789 --> 00:14:43,929
for me, or for anyone else.

229
00:14:44,960 --> 00:14:46,960
You're doing it for yourself.

230
00:14:49,406 --> 00:14:50,969
But that's not entirely true.

231
00:14:51,628 --> 00:14:53,502
Because if it weren't for you,

232
00:14:53,527 --> 00:14:55,700
I wouldn't have thought
about competing again.

233
00:14:56,437 --> 00:14:58,190
As for this competition,

234
00:14:58,215 --> 00:15:01,079
the first thing I want to do
is make you happy.

235
00:15:02,157 --> 00:15:05,910
As for me, I'll just consider
that a little bonus.

236
00:15:05,935 --> 00:15:09,503
I think it's a good thing that
this bonus is an opportunity.

237
00:15:10,027 --> 00:15:13,261
An opportunity to reconnect
with my feelings,

238
00:15:13,286 --> 00:15:15,324
to reconnect with my own heart.

239
00:15:20,742 --> 00:15:23,398
But what if the victory
you're about to win

240
00:15:24,407 --> 00:15:26,407
ends up pulling us apart?

241
00:15:27,554 --> 00:15:28,723
How would it?

242
00:15:31,621 --> 00:15:33,852
If everything goes perfectly,

243
00:15:34,343 --> 00:15:35,777
you win the championship,

244
00:15:36,650 --> 00:15:39,359
and our course
gets to host the Asian Tour,

245
00:15:39,750 --> 00:15:41,411
everything will fall into place.

246
00:15:42,642 --> 00:15:44,721
The course will regain
its reputation,

247
00:15:45,139 --> 00:15:46,892
and turn a profit again.

248
00:15:48,805 --> 00:15:50,805
And I'll go back to France.

249
00:15:52,535 --> 00:15:54,853
That's all in the future.

250
00:15:54,892 --> 00:15:58,005
But right now,
you're still here with me.

251
00:16:03,470 --> 00:16:05,682
Let me do this for you first.

252
00:16:06,102 --> 00:16:08,904
And I'll give it
everything I've got.

253
00:16:11,214 --> 00:16:12,897
Thank you, Vee.

254
00:16:14,350 --> 00:16:17,404
♪ But tell me,
why should we care? ♪

255
00:16:17,429 --> 00:16:20,030
♪ When all we need
is love that's fair ♪

256
00:16:20,055 --> 00:16:24,149
♪ In a love we share,
no one has to win or lose ♪

257
00:16:24,174 --> 00:16:29,660
♪ Even when the storm rolls in
or tears fill your eyes ♪

258
00:16:30,276 --> 00:16:34,321
♪ Turn around, you'll find me
right by your side ♪

259
00:16:34,347 --> 00:16:37,995
♪ Even when the whole world
turns unkind ♪

260
00:16:38,020 --> 00:16:40,418
♪ You won't be left behind ♪

261
00:16:40,443 --> 00:16:45,342
♪ Cause I'll always be right here
by your side ♪

262
00:17:21,792 --> 00:17:23,755
It's good to have
a pro like her back.

263
00:17:23,780 --> 00:17:26,175
I was a little disappointed
when she left.

264
00:17:27,083 --> 00:17:28,974
She's a talented pro.

265
00:17:30,474 --> 00:17:31,723
What's her name again?

266
00:17:32,791 --> 00:17:33,869
Pro Jin.

267
00:17:35,076 --> 00:17:38,187
Jinny, who's fueled
by resentment.

268
00:17:39,733 --> 00:17:43,543
And that resentment will bring
our course the victory.

269
00:17:44,848 --> 00:17:47,089
Good. That's clever.

270
00:17:48,298 --> 00:17:51,665
Turn that anger and resentment
into a weapon.

271
00:17:52,570 --> 00:17:54,851
Someone who competes
with that kind of emotion

272
00:17:54,876 --> 00:17:56,518
won't give up easily.

273
00:17:57,149 --> 00:17:58,775
See? Now you understand,
Ms. Yupadee.

274
00:17:59,350 --> 00:18:01,716
I've got everything
planned out.

275
00:18:02,596 --> 00:18:05,742
Enough talk. It's just a plan.

276
00:18:06,362 --> 00:18:08,048
I'm waiting to see results.

277
00:18:11,600 --> 00:18:12,660
You have my word.

278
00:18:13,112 --> 00:18:15,152
I've got
plenty of backup plans, too.

279
00:18:41,547 --> 00:18:44,041
Hiding over there?
You think I can't see you?

280
00:18:48,507 --> 00:18:51,200
I didn't want to distract you.

281
00:18:52,365 --> 00:18:53,510
You wouldn't distract me.

282
00:18:54,223 --> 00:18:57,078
In fact, you make me want
to practice even harder.

283
00:18:58,039 --> 00:19:01,471
Then here. Some motivation
you can actually eat.

284
00:19:01,496 --> 00:19:04,562
Hmm, but...

285
00:19:04,587 --> 00:19:08,081
Looks like you'll have to
feed me yourself.

286
00:19:10,061 --> 00:19:11,179
Sure.

287
00:19:11,434 --> 00:19:13,761
Here... nom!

288
00:19:19,249 --> 00:19:20,627
Mmm.

289
00:19:24,930 --> 00:19:26,484
Sweeter than I expected.

290
00:19:26,509 --> 00:19:27,667
The dessert?

291
00:19:27,692 --> 00:19:29,135
The one feeding me.

292
00:19:29,160 --> 00:19:31,160
Sweet and fragrant.

293
00:19:32,023 --> 00:19:33,648
Can I have another kiss?

294
00:19:33,673 --> 00:19:35,889
It'll give me the motivation
to keep practicing.

295
00:19:36,508 --> 00:19:38,537
A golfer this good
at sweet-talking...

296
00:19:38,562 --> 00:19:39,998
Besides winning the championship,

297
00:19:40,023 --> 00:19:42,824
you're going to win all
four chambers of my heart, too.

298
00:19:44,421 --> 00:19:45,456
Hmm?

299
00:19:47,885 --> 00:19:48,976
Want another bite?

300
00:19:50,971 --> 00:19:52,170
Hmm.

301
00:19:54,156 --> 00:19:56,538
Mmm, this tastes even better.

302
00:19:57,302 --> 00:20:00,493
I'll feed you. Nom!

303
00:20:01,274 --> 00:20:02,466
Want to share?

304
00:20:06,491 --> 00:20:11,020
Mmm-hmm. It's so sweet.

305
00:20:11,315 --> 00:20:14,509
Even tastier, tastier, tastier!

306
00:20:15,688 --> 00:20:16,711
Here.

307
00:20:17,384 --> 00:20:19,124
I haven't even finished chewing.

308
00:20:30,277 --> 00:20:31,648
You're so good.

309
00:20:31,673 --> 00:20:35,143
♪ Everyone can tell by the way you stare ♪
You got this!

310
00:20:35,875 --> 00:20:37,741
♪ Sneaking little looks
when I'm unaware ♪

311
00:20:37,766 --> 00:20:43,493
♪ It's plain to see ♪
♪ I know exactly
what you think of me ♪

312
00:20:43,518 --> 00:20:46,878
♪ First to watch my stories
every time ♪

313
00:20:47,525 --> 00:20:49,158
♪ You remember
every fave of mine ♪
Thank you.

314
00:20:49,191 --> 00:20:51,191
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

315
00:20:52,913 --> 00:20:54,989
♪ Don't tell me
there's nothing on your mind ♪

316
00:20:55,014 --> 00:20:57,873
♪ So when are you
gonna say the words? ♪

317
00:20:57,898 --> 00:20:59,867
♪ Don't keep me waiting
till it hurts ♪

318
00:20:59,892 --> 00:21:02,680
♪ The way you act,
I know you're into me ♪

319
00:21:02,705 --> 00:21:05,541
♪ That racing heart
gives you away so easily ♪

320
00:21:05,566 --> 00:21:09,359
♪ But I'll play clueless,
just wait and see ♪

321
00:21:09,384 --> 00:21:11,333
♪ I wanna hear you say it to me ♪

322
00:21:11,341 --> 00:21:14,266
♪ Giving me signs,
so why still wait? ♪

323
00:21:14,291 --> 00:21:17,659
♪ You know I'm into you, I bet ♪

324
00:21:17,684 --> 00:21:22,421
♪ How long will you keep
playing so tough? ♪

325
00:21:22,446 --> 00:21:24,552
♪ Or should I be the one
to call your bluff? ♪

326
00:21:25,911 --> 00:21:27,019
Here, have some water.

327
00:21:27,043 --> 00:21:29,718
♪ Call it just a little crush♪
But you don't hide it well enough♪

328
00:21:29,743 --> 00:21:32,642
♪ Say that there's nothing on your mind
But no one's buying that little lie ♪

329
00:21:32,667 --> 00:21:33,900
You got this!

330
00:21:33,925 --> 00:21:35,408
- Thanks.
- Fighting!

331
00:21:38,045 --> 00:21:39,108
Great job.

332
00:21:42,602 --> 00:21:44,643
Hey, isn't that my water?

333
00:21:45,048 --> 00:21:46,303
It's hot and I'm thirsty, too.

334
00:21:48,025 --> 00:21:49,408
Thanks.

335
00:21:52,955 --> 00:21:54,141
(Belle - Jinny)

336
00:21:54,803 --> 00:21:57,914
♪ Giving me signs,
so why still wait? ♪

337
00:21:57,939 --> 00:22:01,362
♪ You know I'm into you, I bet ♪

338
00:22:01,387 --> 00:22:05,199
♪ How long will you keep
playing so tough? ♪

339
00:22:05,224 --> 00:22:08,364
Hello. This event is
full of talented pros.

340
00:22:08,389 --> 00:22:10,541
- He'll be here. We'll talk then.
- Hello. Please, come.

341
00:22:13,715 --> 00:22:15,812
- Oh, Uncle. Hello.
- Oh, Nana.

342
00:22:15,837 --> 00:22:16,961
Hello, sweetheart.

343
00:22:16,986 --> 00:22:18,985
Wow, what a lucky day.

344
00:22:19,010 --> 00:22:21,226
I get to see
the talented CEO of this place.

345
00:22:21,251 --> 00:22:23,824
I've known you
since you were little,

346
00:22:23,849 --> 00:22:25,849
running around here all the time.

347
00:22:26,234 --> 00:22:27,887
Here you go. Please, come in.

348
00:22:27,912 --> 00:22:30,865
I'm actually organizing
a golf tournament here.

349
00:22:31,237 --> 00:22:34,512
Oh, wow. What a shame.

350
00:22:34,537 --> 00:22:36,862
It's the same day
as my eye surgery.

351
00:22:36,887 --> 00:22:39,214
- Maybe next time.
- Sure.

352
00:22:39,239 --> 00:22:43,115
Oh, by the way, your father
has started his chemo, right?

353
00:22:45,003 --> 00:22:46,407
- Chemo?
- Mm-hmm.

354
00:23:00,753 --> 00:23:02,523
Oh, August, my boy.

355
00:23:04,814 --> 00:23:08,356
Looks like the CEO called you in
for an emergency meeting, too?

356
00:23:23,255 --> 00:23:26,751
What's wrong? Why do you two
look so serious?

357
00:23:26,751 --> 00:23:28,449
What's going on, kids?

358
00:23:29,081 --> 00:23:30,556
Come on, tell me.

359
00:23:30,581 --> 00:23:32,984
Why did you call me here
so urgently?

360
00:23:51,223 --> 00:23:52,262
What's wrong, kids?

361
00:23:54,519 --> 00:23:55,940
- Dad.
- Hmm?

362
00:23:57,642 --> 00:24:00,126
Is there something
you need to tell us?

363
00:24:03,527 --> 00:24:05,585
Why are you asking me
such strange questions?

364
00:24:05,610 --> 00:24:07,347
What do you want me to say?

365
00:24:10,646 --> 00:24:13,782
Something the two of us
should know about.

366
00:24:18,820 --> 00:24:23,023
Oh, you mean the land
I bought in Khao Yai?

367
00:24:23,048 --> 00:24:25,384
- Or the mine...
- Your cancer.

368
00:24:38,777 --> 00:24:40,088
Who told you?

369
00:24:46,119 --> 00:24:47,713
Why didn't you tell us, Dad?

370
00:24:50,918 --> 00:24:53,954
I was afraid you'd both
end up like this.

371
00:24:55,454 --> 00:24:56,890
But don't worry, sweetheart.

372
00:24:57,654 --> 00:25:00,166
I'm about
to start my chemo treatment.

373
00:25:04,015 --> 00:25:05,077
When?

374
00:25:06,339 --> 00:25:07,935
Soon.

375
00:25:16,062 --> 00:25:17,674
I love you, Dad.

376
00:25:21,575 --> 00:25:23,220
I love you, too, Dad.

377
00:25:26,779 --> 00:25:28,226
I love you both, too.

378
00:25:32,389 --> 00:25:33,755
I promise.

379
00:25:35,118 --> 00:25:39,310
I'll get the best treatment
they have to offer.

380
00:25:46,798 --> 00:25:49,115
It's okay, sweetheart. Don't cry.

381
00:25:50,522 --> 00:25:53,254
Look at your old man.
I'm still strong and healthy.

382
00:25:53,279 --> 00:25:54,994
I look this healthy,

383
00:25:55,019 --> 00:25:58,624
no one would ever know I had
cancer if I didn't tell them.

384
00:25:59,095 --> 00:26:00,230
Right?

385
00:26:04,362 --> 00:26:05,378
It's okay, sweetheart.

386
00:26:14,830 --> 00:26:16,540
- Here you go.
- Thank you.

387
00:26:21,315 --> 00:26:23,255
Aren't you worried
they'll tamper with your drink?

388
00:26:25,060 --> 00:26:26,791
Is that really
all you can think of?

389
00:26:44,347 --> 00:26:46,231
Thank you all so much.

390
00:26:46,256 --> 00:26:48,274
I know
how hard everyone's been working

391
00:26:48,299 --> 00:26:49,958
to make this event
the best it can be.

392
00:26:49,982 --> 00:26:51,133
And it has to be.

393
00:26:51,713 --> 00:26:53,244
We're not just aiming
for the All Star.

394
00:26:53,269 --> 00:26:55,218
We're aiming for the Asian Tour.

395
00:26:55,337 --> 00:26:57,526
Does anyone have anything
to add today?

396
00:26:59,803 --> 00:27:00,820
Anyone?

397
00:27:01,940 --> 00:27:03,600
Thank you all for today.

398
00:27:03,838 --> 00:27:05,243
Wait, Miss!

399
00:27:05,268 --> 00:27:07,325
Shouldn't we have a little
"Vive la vie"?

400
00:27:08,120 --> 00:27:09,224
Vive la vie!

401
00:27:09,249 --> 00:27:11,933
- Vive la vie!
- Vive la vie!

402
00:27:23,819 --> 00:27:25,972
An army marches on its stomach!

403
00:27:25,997 --> 00:27:27,997
Eat up, everyone,
then let's get back to work.

404
00:27:28,022 --> 00:27:29,086
Go ahead and hand them out.

405
00:27:29,269 --> 00:27:32,223
- Wow!
- Wow!

406
00:27:33,386 --> 00:27:35,148
That looks delicious.

407
00:27:35,173 --> 00:27:36,999
- Chef, slacking off today?
- Thanks.

408
00:28:08,710 --> 00:28:10,321
De-li-ciousss!

409
00:28:15,860 --> 00:28:17,812
All right, let's go.
We should split up.

410
00:28:17,837 --> 00:28:20,083
Ooh, I've got a lot
to take care of over there.

411
00:28:27,299 --> 00:28:30,817
Oh, I'm thinking of
going home tonight.

412
00:28:30,842 --> 00:28:32,118
To see your mom?

413
00:28:33,239 --> 00:28:36,237
Then give my regards to your mom.

414
00:28:36,262 --> 00:28:38,262
Is she coming
to the All Star event?

415
00:28:38,287 --> 00:28:42,027
Definitely. I hear she's already
picked out her outfit.

416
00:28:42,052 --> 00:28:45,626
Good. You'll have enough support
to fill the whole course.

417
00:28:45,658 --> 00:28:47,941
Are you staying
at your mom's tonight?

418
00:28:47,966 --> 00:28:51,680
Hmm, I'm not sure yet.
I'll see how things go first.

419
00:28:51,705 --> 00:28:54,320
Then I'll eat dinner here tonight
instead of waiting for you.

420
00:28:55,289 --> 00:28:57,582
I'll let you know later
whether I'm staying or not.

421
00:28:57,607 --> 00:28:58,656
Okay.

422
00:29:13,285 --> 00:29:15,134
You've seen
what Pro Jin can do, right?

423
00:29:15,159 --> 00:29:15,943
Mm-hmm.

424
00:29:17,153 --> 00:29:18,732
I picked
the right person, didn't I?

425
00:29:20,039 --> 00:29:21,795
With her in this kind of form,

426
00:29:21,820 --> 00:29:24,168
she should have no trouble
beating the competition.

427
00:29:24,564 --> 00:29:25,580
For me,

428
00:29:26,395 --> 00:29:27,949
it's not enough
to put up a fight.

429
00:29:27,974 --> 00:29:29,409
We have to win.

430
00:29:31,594 --> 00:29:34,599
If we get to host the Asian Tour,

431
00:29:35,433 --> 00:29:36,597
just think about

432
00:29:36,622 --> 00:29:40,788
how many more people will see
what our course is capable of.

433
00:29:40,813 --> 00:29:42,339
That's my goal.

434
00:29:45,723 --> 00:29:46,764
Yes, ma'am.

435
00:29:47,439 --> 00:29:49,764
The only pro
who can really match Pro Jin

436
00:29:50,106 --> 00:29:52,586
is probably
Pro Vee from Goodview.

437
00:29:52,650 --> 00:29:54,022
Don't get complacent.

438
00:29:54,615 --> 00:29:56,569
It wouldn't hurt
to have a backup plan.

439
00:29:57,531 --> 00:29:58,587
Yes, ma'am.

440
00:29:59,024 --> 00:30:01,650
I'm pretty good at playing dirty.

441
00:30:06,526 --> 00:30:09,334
- Have a seat, Pro Jin.
- Thank you.

442
00:30:15,926 --> 00:30:19,718
I want you to bring home
the All Star championship.

443
00:30:19,743 --> 00:30:21,276
By any means necessary.

444
00:30:21,301 --> 00:30:24,303
Of course.
We have to win this match.

445
00:30:24,655 --> 00:30:27,893
Good. I like that attitude.

446
00:30:30,046 --> 00:30:33,915
Oh, and I'd like to ask you to...

447
00:30:33,940 --> 00:30:36,110
stay away
from the people at Goodview.

448
00:30:36,579 --> 00:30:38,025
What does that
have to do with anything?

449
00:30:38,398 --> 00:30:41,921
They might send that Belle
to snoop around our course.

450
00:30:43,509 --> 00:30:46,912
People on the other side
will never truly be on our side.

451
00:30:47,999 --> 00:30:49,629
The closer we get to them,

452
00:30:50,670 --> 00:30:51,902
the greater the risk.

453
00:30:53,061 --> 00:30:55,394
People who see
their rivals as enemies

454
00:30:55,743 --> 00:30:57,798
often miss the opportunities
right in front of them.

455
00:30:57,823 --> 00:31:01,435
Because sometimes, getting close
gives us a chance

456
00:31:01,460 --> 00:31:03,264
to see what they're hiding.

457
00:31:04,286 --> 00:31:05,691
Just like this time.

458
00:31:06,154 --> 00:31:08,674
I let her compete for Goodview

459
00:31:09,070 --> 00:31:10,113
because normally,

460
00:31:10,138 --> 00:31:13,677
we'd never get to see
every corner of their course.

461
00:31:13,701 --> 00:31:15,185
But this competition

462
00:31:15,210 --> 00:31:19,858
will give us a chance to see
every corner of their operation.

463
00:31:20,186 --> 00:31:23,290
Work with me.
Don't think so narrowly.

464
00:31:23,315 --> 00:31:24,936
Don't disappoint me.

465
00:31:26,717 --> 00:31:30,663
People only remember first place.
No one remembers second.

466
00:31:58,407 --> 00:32:00,280
(Eat it while it's still hot.)

467
00:32:31,551 --> 00:32:34,632
Go ahead and season it
to your liking. Okay?

468
00:32:37,749 --> 00:32:40,505
Oh, Pro Jin!
What brings you here?

469
00:32:41,204 --> 00:32:42,362
What a coincidence.

470
00:32:45,776 --> 00:32:46,871
Coincidence?

471
00:32:46,896 --> 00:32:49,554
Oops. Belle must've tagged
the wrong person.

472
00:32:50,866 --> 00:32:54,782
Well, since I'm already here,
mind if I join you?

473
00:32:55,465 --> 00:32:56,543
Please.

474
00:33:01,374 --> 00:33:02,469
Have you ordered yet?

475
00:33:02,494 --> 00:33:05,136
Not yet.
What would you like, Pro Jin?

476
00:33:05,161 --> 00:33:06,335
The usual.

477
00:33:07,066 --> 00:33:08,092
- Uncle.
- Yes?

478
00:33:08,117 --> 00:33:09,719
Two dry chicken noodle soups,
please.

479
00:33:09,744 --> 00:33:10,893
And two bowls of broth, please.

480
00:33:10,918 --> 00:33:13,504
Oh, the usual. Coming right up.

481
00:33:13,599 --> 00:33:15,218
Are you ready
for the competition?

482
00:33:15,805 --> 00:33:19,364
Very. This time, I'm going
to beat Pro Vee.

483
00:33:19,389 --> 00:33:21,264
I want to cheer you on, too.

484
00:33:21,962 --> 00:33:23,645
But if you win,

485
00:33:23,670 --> 00:33:27,134
that means Goodview won't get
the right to host the Asian Tour.

486
00:33:27,663 --> 00:33:30,508
But if I cheer for
Pro Vee and Goodview,

487
00:33:30,533 --> 00:33:32,191
that means you have to lose.

488
00:33:32,962 --> 00:33:35,027
And I don't want that either.

489
00:33:35,547 --> 00:33:38,197
Even if our courses are rivals,

490
00:33:38,222 --> 00:33:39,890
you and I aren't.

491
00:33:39,915 --> 00:33:41,915
If you cheer for me that openly,

492
00:33:42,217 --> 00:33:43,997
you might need to find a new job.

493
00:33:45,627 --> 00:33:48,905
Then I'll just choose to believe

494
00:33:48,930 --> 00:33:51,726
that whenever I look over
and see you by the sidelines,

495
00:33:52,117 --> 00:33:54,117
you're cheering me on
in your heart.

496
00:34:00,264 --> 00:34:03,620
Here you go. Two noodles.

497
00:34:03,773 --> 00:34:09,076
And two bowls of broth,
just like usual.

498
00:34:10,033 --> 00:34:12,867
Oh, and this...

499
00:34:17,615 --> 00:34:18,931
We didn't order this.

500
00:34:18,956 --> 00:34:20,844
A pair of shumai. On the house.

501
00:34:20,869 --> 00:34:22,553
To make you two a pair sooner.

502
00:34:39,067 --> 00:34:40,358
Is this too big?

503
00:35:16,768 --> 00:35:17,898
Nana.

504
00:35:18,789 --> 00:35:20,131
Vee...

505
00:35:20,570 --> 00:35:23,848
What's wrong?
Why are you covered in a rash?

506
00:35:23,873 --> 00:35:25,516
The soup you brought me...

507
00:35:25,541 --> 00:35:27,599
Did it have shrimp in it?

508
00:35:28,821 --> 00:35:29,980
What soup?

509
00:35:30,005 --> 00:35:32,476
The soup you left
outside my house.

510
00:35:40,284 --> 00:35:42,996
Nana. Nana!

511
00:35:43,631 --> 00:35:44,678
Nana!

512
00:35:49,963 --> 00:35:52,788
You're okay now. I've already
given you an injection.

513
00:35:52,813 --> 00:35:54,177
You probably only ate a little.

514
00:35:54,771 --> 00:35:56,428
Just two or three bites.

515
00:35:57,294 --> 00:36:00,246
You should stay overnight
so we can monitor you.

516
00:36:00,681 --> 00:36:03,823
If there are no further symptoms,
you can go home tomorrow.

517
00:36:04,958 --> 00:36:07,257
Be careful about what you eat
from now on.

518
00:36:07,282 --> 00:36:10,457
And when you have time,
come back for an allergy test.

519
00:36:10,769 --> 00:36:12,135
You might be allergic
to something else, too.

520
00:36:13,978 --> 00:36:15,708
- Okay.
- All right.

521
00:36:17,067 --> 00:36:18,640
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

522
00:36:49,745 --> 00:36:50,954
Are you coming inside?

523
00:36:52,384 --> 00:36:53,670
Probably not a good idea.

524
00:36:54,726 --> 00:36:58,190
Someone from a rival course
coming into my house this late...

525
00:36:59,575 --> 00:37:00,654
You're right.

526
00:37:02,330 --> 00:37:03,745
Thank you.

527
00:37:03,770 --> 00:37:06,229
For what?

528
00:37:07,967 --> 00:37:13,332
For the food you sent,
the messages,

529
00:37:13,797 --> 00:37:15,955
and the support.

530
00:37:26,206 --> 00:37:28,359
I wonder what will happen to us.

531
00:37:29,136 --> 00:37:30,898
What do you want to happen?

532
00:37:35,106 --> 00:37:36,272
I don't know.

533
00:37:37,026 --> 00:37:40,164
Why don't we figure that out
after the All Star?

534
00:37:40,734 --> 00:37:43,629
Right now, we should focus on
the competition

535
00:37:43,654 --> 00:37:45,169
you've been waiting for.

536
00:37:47,269 --> 00:37:48,474
If I win...

537
00:37:49,492 --> 00:37:51,143
what happens after that?

538
00:37:52,483 --> 00:37:53,870
And if I lose...

539
00:37:55,570 --> 00:37:57,705
Let's leave that for the future.

540
00:37:58,968 --> 00:38:03,631
For now, let this be your answer.

541
00:39:48,456 --> 00:39:49,841
Thank you, Vee.

542
00:39:50,906 --> 00:39:54,132
I had someone
check the CCTV footage.

543
00:39:54,157 --> 00:39:56,464
The person
who left the soup for you

544
00:39:56,489 --> 00:40:00,240
was wearing a helmet and dressed
like an ordinary delivery driver,

545
00:40:00,265 --> 00:40:02,222
so they got in easily.

546
00:40:02,247 --> 00:40:03,937
We couldn't see their face,

547
00:40:03,977 --> 00:40:05,683
and we couldn't see
the license plate either.

548
00:40:07,305 --> 00:40:09,767
Could they have delivered it
to the wrong house?

549
00:40:10,918 --> 00:40:13,191
I wish I could believe that, too.

550
00:40:13,216 --> 00:40:15,296
That it was just
a delivery mix-up,

551
00:40:15,321 --> 00:40:17,321
and it just happened to
contain shrimp.

552
00:40:18,078 --> 00:40:19,355
From now on,

553
00:40:19,380 --> 00:40:22,058
you need to be much more careful.
Understand?

554
00:40:23,185 --> 00:40:25,185
Don't worry about me, Vee.

555
00:40:25,210 --> 00:40:26,786
I'll be fine.

556
00:40:26,811 --> 00:40:28,550
The competition is almost here.

557
00:40:28,575 --> 00:40:30,828
I don't want you to lose focus.

558
00:40:30,853 --> 00:40:32,958
I don't want to become
a burden to you.

559
00:40:35,359 --> 00:40:38,153
You've never been a burden to me.

560
00:40:38,634 --> 00:40:42,562
You're the reason I have to win.

561
00:40:45,147 --> 00:40:48,649
How are you feeling now?
Any better?

562
00:40:49,030 --> 00:40:51,482
I felt better
the moment I saw you.

563
00:40:51,527 --> 00:40:54,375
I always feel safe
when you're with me.

564
00:40:57,792 --> 00:41:01,623
Oh, you're really good
at sweet-talking me.

565
00:41:02,043 --> 00:41:05,637
Is this part of your plan
to make me fall for you?

566
00:41:06,757 --> 00:41:07,821
Oh, come on, Vee...

567
00:41:08,606 --> 00:41:10,276
I'm just teasing you.

568
00:41:10,301 --> 00:41:13,811
I already know that
someone this cute,

569
00:41:13,836 --> 00:41:19,370
with this face, this smile,
and these eyes...

570
00:41:19,847 --> 00:41:22,778
doesn't have to charm me.
I'm already head over heels.

571
00:41:25,687 --> 00:41:28,136
Come on.
You should get some sleep.

572
00:41:29,446 --> 00:41:30,541
Get some proper rest.

573
00:41:32,066 --> 00:41:34,462
So you'll wake up
feeling refreshed tomorrow.

574
00:41:34,629 --> 00:41:35,724
Now close your eyes.

575
00:41:36,666 --> 00:41:38,653
Tell me a bedtime story.

576
00:41:38,812 --> 00:41:40,812
Hmm? A bedtime story?

577
00:41:41,204 --> 00:41:43,442
Your mom told me that
when we were little,

578
00:41:43,467 --> 00:41:45,270
whenever I stayed over
at your house,

579
00:41:45,295 --> 00:41:47,670
you'd tell me stories
until I fell asleep.

580
00:41:47,695 --> 00:41:50,877
Wow. Now that you know
you can get your way with me,

581
00:41:50,902 --> 00:41:52,663
you're really going for it.

582
00:41:53,440 --> 00:41:54,669
Rub my hand too, please?

583
00:41:57,984 --> 00:42:01,065
Hmm. What story
would you like to hear?

584
00:42:01,398 --> 00:42:02,525
Anything.

585
00:42:05,463 --> 00:42:10,251
Once upon a time, long, long ago,

586
00:42:10,276 --> 00:42:12,737
there lived two princesses.

587
00:42:12,762 --> 00:42:14,849
A wicked wizard tricked them

588
00:42:14,874 --> 00:42:16,574
into venturing
deep into the forest,

589
00:42:16,598 --> 00:42:18,805
then locked them away
in a little cottage.

590
00:42:28,091 --> 00:42:31,256
♪ Promise you'll stay
close to me ♪

591
00:42:31,281 --> 00:42:33,717
♪ Hold me in your arms
so tenderly ♪

592
00:42:33,742 --> 00:42:39,350
♪ I've never bowed
to anyone in sight ♪

593
00:42:39,375 --> 00:42:42,410
♪ But for you,
I'd surrender without a fight ♪

594
00:42:42,435 --> 00:42:46,707
♪ Just take my hand
and hold it tight ♪

595
00:42:48,574 --> 00:42:51,666
♪ And walk with me
along the way ♪

596
00:42:51,691 --> 00:42:54,350
♪ No matter what it takes
to win someday ♪

597
00:42:54,375 --> 00:43:00,014
♪ Sometimes this tender heart
may despair ♪

598
00:43:00,039 --> 00:43:03,169
♪ But tell me,
why should we care? ♪

599
00:43:03,194 --> 00:43:05,704
♪ When all we need
is love that's fair ♪

600
00:43:05,729 --> 00:43:09,319
♪ In a love we share,
no one has to win or lose ♪

601
00:43:16,071 --> 00:43:17,222
Have a seat.

602
00:43:22,114 --> 00:43:23,836
I called you here

603
00:43:23,861 --> 00:43:25,987
because I want everything
to go according to plan.

604
00:43:27,463 --> 00:43:28,560
What plan?

605
00:43:29,959 --> 00:43:32,070
The plan to make sure you win
the championship tomorrow.

606
00:43:34,126 --> 00:43:35,618
I don't like
leaving things to chance.

607
00:43:36,332 --> 00:43:39,918
I want to know for certain,
before you even compete,

608
00:43:39,943 --> 00:43:41,344
that you're going to win.

609
00:43:44,052 --> 00:43:47,564
This is a ball drop device.
Just strap it to your ankle.

610
00:43:47,589 --> 00:43:50,292
If your ball gets stuck
in an unplayable hazard,

611
00:43:51,412 --> 00:43:52,556
just tap it lightly,

612
00:43:52,581 --> 00:43:53,796
and a new ball will drop out.

613
00:43:55,068 --> 00:43:57,999
And this is a rangefinder
I modified myself.

614
00:43:58,024 --> 00:44:00,944
You can use its slope mode
without anyone noticing.

615
00:44:01,774 --> 00:44:03,791
But slope mode
is against the rules.

616
00:44:04,711 --> 00:44:05,862
So is the ball drop device.

617
00:44:07,418 --> 00:44:09,493
But we're not talking about
right or wrong here.

618
00:44:10,855 --> 00:44:12,425
We're talking about winning.

619
00:44:14,907 --> 00:44:18,170
So The Royal Green doesn't trust
my ability to win on my own.

620
00:44:19,273 --> 00:44:20,622
Like I said,

621
00:44:21,433 --> 00:44:22,715
I don't like
leaving things to chance.

622
00:44:24,009 --> 00:44:25,509
I only like to win.

623
00:44:28,118 --> 00:44:31,183
I've already gone over everything
with your caddie.

624
00:44:31,972 --> 00:44:33,751
Don't forget
to wear long pants tomorrow.

625
00:44:34,274 --> 00:44:35,801
That way,
you can hide the device.

626
00:44:35,865 --> 00:44:38,565
As for the camera,
I'll give it to your caddie.

627
00:44:39,265 --> 00:44:40,273
That's the plan.

628
00:44:56,839 --> 00:44:59,112
Tomorrow is a big day
for our course.

629
00:44:59,137 --> 00:45:03,138
I want to thank everyone
for giving it your all.

630
00:45:03,163 --> 00:45:06,839
The course was once so quiet,
but now it's come back to life.

631
00:45:09,003 --> 00:45:12,155
Tomorrow will be the first step
in proving that

632
00:45:12,180 --> 00:45:15,635
our course can rise to the top
of the golf industry once again.

633
00:45:18,774 --> 00:45:20,340
As for the competition,

634
00:45:20,365 --> 00:45:22,618
we're putting our hopes in you,
Pro Vee.

635
00:45:22,987 --> 00:45:24,947
The road to hosting
the Asian Tour

636
00:45:24,987 --> 00:45:26,093
is now in your hands.

637
00:45:26,117 --> 00:45:28,250
Bring home the win
for our course.

638
00:45:32,566 --> 00:45:33,735
Vive la vie!

639
00:45:34,013 --> 00:45:36,489
- Vive la vie!
- Vive la vie!

640
00:45:53,285 --> 00:45:54,622
Miss.

641
00:45:55,789 --> 00:45:57,037
Can I talk to you?

642
00:45:57,728 --> 00:45:59,299
There's something bothering me.

643
00:45:59,947 --> 00:46:02,509
About what you just said
to Pro Vee...

644
00:46:03,225 --> 00:46:04,871
Don't you think she might feel

645
00:46:04,896 --> 00:46:07,460
like she's carrying the whole
course on her shoulders?

646
00:46:08,015 --> 00:46:09,995
I just believe in Pro Vee.

647
00:46:10,020 --> 00:46:12,188
Believing in her
is a good thing, Miss.

648
00:46:12,213 --> 00:46:14,895
But I wonder
if all that expectation

649
00:46:14,920 --> 00:46:16,920
might feel like too much.

650
00:46:17,097 --> 00:46:20,512
Pro Vee really
is a great pro, Miss.

651
00:46:20,537 --> 00:46:22,444
But if you take a step back,

652
00:46:22,469 --> 00:46:25,772
she's just a petite woman,
just like you, Miss.

653
00:46:28,286 --> 00:46:29,692
You're right.

654
00:46:29,717 --> 00:46:32,384
I'll find a chance
to talk to Pro Vee

655
00:46:32,409 --> 00:46:34,593
so she won't feel so stressed.
How's that?

656
00:46:34,618 --> 00:46:35,715
Good.

657
00:46:36,247 --> 00:46:37,334
Vive la vie!

658
00:46:37,359 --> 00:46:38,525
Vive la vie!

659
00:46:51,682 --> 00:46:53,271
You didn't tag me
by mistake, did you?

660
00:46:53,827 --> 00:46:54,962
I meant to invite you.

661
00:47:00,686 --> 00:47:01,726
Hungry?

662
00:47:02,732 --> 00:47:05,204
The competition's tomorrow.
I need some encouragement.

663
00:47:05,229 --> 00:47:06,347
The usual?

664
00:47:07,074 --> 00:47:09,701
Uncle, two dry chicken noodles,
please.

665
00:47:09,726 --> 00:47:11,100
And two bowls of broth, please.

666
00:47:11,125 --> 00:47:13,125
Oh, the usual. Coming right up.

667
00:47:13,426 --> 00:47:14,486
- Tomorrow...
- Tomorrow...

668
00:47:16,179 --> 00:47:17,282
You go first.

669
00:47:17,831 --> 00:47:20,014
Give it your all tomorrow.

670
00:47:20,039 --> 00:47:21,191
That's all?

671
00:47:21,939 --> 00:47:25,907
Don't forget, tomorrow
we'll still be on opposite sides.

672
00:47:25,932 --> 00:47:28,783
I believe both Goodview
and The Royal Green

673
00:47:28,808 --> 00:47:30,141
will give it their all, too.

674
00:47:30,165 --> 00:47:32,829
And no matter
how the competition turns out,

675
00:47:32,854 --> 00:47:34,854
no matter which side
I have to stand on,

676
00:47:35,582 --> 00:47:38,615
my heart will always be
on your side, Pro Jin.

677
00:47:44,248 --> 00:47:46,642
Here come the noodles!

678
00:47:46,667 --> 00:47:50,507
There you go. All set.

679
00:47:50,634 --> 00:47:52,314
No shumai pair today?

680
00:47:53,084 --> 00:47:55,807
I don't think you need
to pair up anymore.

681
00:47:55,843 --> 00:47:59,813
Looks like you've already...
paired up.

682
00:48:00,137 --> 00:48:04,284
There you go, that sweet smile.
Make yourselves at home.

683
00:48:09,217 --> 00:48:11,320
No matter what happens tomorrow,

684
00:48:12,423 --> 00:48:15,129
- I want to tell you...
- I don't want to hear it yet.

685
00:48:16,923 --> 00:48:19,017
Can I wait
until after the competition?

686
00:48:21,950 --> 00:48:23,378
Let's eat.

687
00:48:23,454 --> 00:48:25,516
You should get to bed
early tonight.

688
00:48:25,723 --> 00:48:27,931
So you're at your best tomorrow.

689
00:48:35,934 --> 00:48:38,435
Here. Eat plenty.

690
00:48:39,072 --> 00:48:40,331
That's enough, don't you think?

691
00:48:40,882 --> 00:48:42,850
You need your strength
for tomorrow.

692
00:48:52,371 --> 00:48:53,768
Still tastes just as good.

693
00:48:54,141 --> 00:48:55,752
Just as good every time.

694
00:49:05,086 --> 00:49:06,195
Vee...

695
00:49:07,203 --> 00:49:09,846
About what I said
at the meeting this afternoon...

696
00:49:10,063 --> 00:49:12,748
Did it make you feel pressured?

697
00:49:13,811 --> 00:49:15,121
What do you mean?

698
00:49:15,567 --> 00:49:17,274
When I made it sound like

699
00:49:17,299 --> 00:49:19,656
you had to carry everything
on your own,

700
00:49:19,681 --> 00:49:23,081
the whole course
and all my hopes.

701
00:49:24,217 --> 00:49:28,078
Mm. It was a little overwhelming,

702
00:49:28,103 --> 00:49:30,495
but I understand you, Nana.

703
00:49:30,535 --> 00:49:31,940
And more importantly,

704
00:49:31,964 --> 00:49:34,045
I'm not carrying anything
on my shoulders.

705
00:49:34,671 --> 00:49:36,480
I'm choosing to do this,

706
00:49:36,505 --> 00:49:38,375
and I'll give it
everything I've got.

707
00:49:38,446 --> 00:49:39,854
Not because anyone forced me to.

708
00:49:41,745 --> 00:49:44,459
And I believe you'll do it, Vee.

709
00:49:44,484 --> 00:49:46,607
I'll be cheering you on
all the way.

710
00:49:48,234 --> 00:49:50,234
What if I lose?

711
00:49:50,262 --> 00:49:53,073
Then you lose.
It's a competition.

712
00:49:53,255 --> 00:49:56,854
What's more important is that
you get to be yourself again.

713
00:49:57,562 --> 00:49:59,160
Be myself again?

714
00:49:59,604 --> 00:50:02,146
To find happiness again
in what you love.

715
00:50:02,297 --> 00:50:05,459
To be brave enough to compete,
without being stuck in the past,

716
00:50:05,484 --> 00:50:07,484
and stop running from yourself.

717
00:50:10,130 --> 00:50:13,959
And if I had to choose between
the course and your feelings,

718
00:50:14,514 --> 00:50:16,022
I'd choose you.

719
00:50:18,309 --> 00:50:19,393
Thank you.

720
00:50:39,299 --> 00:50:40,688
That's enough.

721
00:50:40,712 --> 00:50:43,338
You won't have any energy left
tomorrow, then blame me.

722
00:51:02,803 --> 00:51:04,895
Hurry up and prove to me

723
00:51:04,920 --> 00:51:08,199
that our course will win
before the 18th hole.

724
00:51:10,147 --> 00:51:13,023
And finally,
representing our course,

725
00:51:13,048 --> 00:51:17,542
Pro Venus
from Goodview Golf Club!

726
00:51:21,472 --> 00:51:24,351
When you love someone,
you don't hold them back.

727
00:51:24,376 --> 00:51:26,705
You help push each other forward,

728
00:51:26,730 --> 00:51:28,523
so the person you love
can reach their dreams,

729
00:51:28,548 --> 00:51:30,055
just like I did for you.

730
00:51:34,036 --> 00:51:38,452
♪ Do you know which way to go? ♪

731
00:51:38,837 --> 00:51:43,903
♪ To get us closer to our goal ♪

732
00:51:43,928 --> 00:51:49,306
♪ Together, we'll race
toward the line ♪

733
00:51:49,331 --> 00:51:54,462
♪ Chasing the dream
that's yours and mine ♪

734
00:51:54,487 --> 00:51:59,529
♪ In the end,
I know we'll make it there ♪

735
00:51:59,554 --> 00:52:04,680
♪ Just one rule
for you and me to share ♪

736
00:52:04,705 --> 00:52:07,787
♪ Promise you'll stay
close to me ♪

737
00:52:07,812 --> 00:52:10,296
♪ Hold me in your arms
so tenderly ♪

738
00:52:10,321 --> 00:52:15,905
♪ I've never bowed
to anyone in sight ♪

739
00:52:15,930 --> 00:52:19,053
♪ But for you,
I'd surrender without a fight ♪

740
00:52:19,078 --> 00:52:23,793
♪ Just take my hand
and hold it tight ♪

741
00:52:25,076 --> 00:52:28,298
♪ And walk with me
along the way ♪

742
00:52:28,323 --> 00:52:30,899
♪ No matter what it takes
to win someday ♪

743
00:52:30,924 --> 00:52:36,515
♪ Sometimes this tender heart
may despair ♪

744
00:52:36,540 --> 00:52:39,780
♪ But tell me,
why should we care? ♪

745
00:52:39,805 --> 00:52:42,204
♪ When all we need
is love that's fair ♪

746
00:52:42,229 --> 00:52:45,943
♪ In a love we share,
no one has to win or lose ♪

747
00:52:47,900 --> 00:52:52,593
♪ Let my heart answer anew ♪

748
00:52:53,133 --> 00:52:58,282
♪ A thousand rounds,
it'd still choose you ♪

749
00:52:58,307 --> 00:53:02,063
♪ One look in your eyes
is all I need ♪
